window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b320-9cff48be71697082.json"]={sha256:"9cff48be716970823943087073e61018f16f7610088cbe9e51db106acda4737b",value:{"id":"b320","title":"雅萬高速鐵路","titleEn":"Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以雅加達至萬隆高速鐵路為背景，建立熱帶丘陵中的橋隧連續路線及接駁旅程。學徒從降雨、坡度和曲線開始，延伸到車站轉乘與需求批次到達，要求把列車行車時間和門到門旅程時間分別驗證。","summaryEn":"Use the Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway to construct a tropical hillside route with successive bridges, tunnels and feeder journeys. Begin with rainfall, gradients and curves, then extend the analysis to station interchange and batch arrivals. Verify train running time separately from door-to-door journey time so that fast line-haul service is not mistaken for a complete passenger-experience result.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-highspeed","subcategoryTitle":"高速鐵路系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"High-speed rail systems","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-highspeed","learningTags":["rail","rail-highspeed","rail"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["路線與土建","Alignment and civil works"],["車輛與接觸","Vehicle and contact"],["牽引供電","Traction supply"],["行車控制","Movement control"],["車站與旅客","Stations and passengers"],["監測與維護","Monitoring and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,1],[3,4],[4,5],[5,0],[5,3]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["路線與土建","車輛與接觸","牽引供電","行車控制","車站與旅客"],"labelsEn":["Alignment and civil works","Vehicle and contact","Traction supply","Movement control","Stations and passengers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合原創算例：單元 1 得 deflection=1.103997 mm；單元 2 得 gradient=0.63 mm/m；單元 3 得 flow=0.3213 m^3/s。上述三個結果使用各單元明示的不同邊界，不能任意相加或視為實際工程實測值。以第一單元 L 的擾動測試，結果改為 1.616362 mm；學徒需先比較單位、敏感度和假設，再決定是否要細化模型。以雅加達至萬隆高速鐵路為背景，建立熱帶丘陵中的橋隧連續路線及接駁旅程。學徒從降雨、坡度和曲線開始，延伸到車站轉乘與需求批次到達，要求把列車行車時間和門到門旅程時間分別驗證。 最終交付應保留原始輸入、測點時間戳、誤差範圍與無法由簡化式證明的結論。","textEn":"Integrated original exercise: unit 1 gives deflection=1.103997 mm; unit 2 gives gradient=0.63 mm/m; unit 3 gives flow=0.3213 m^3/s. These three results use different explicit boundaries and must not be added or presented as measurements of the real railway. Perturbing L in the first unit changes its result to 1.616362 mm. Compare units, sensitivity and assumptions before deciding which model needs refinement. Use the Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway to construct a tropical hillside route with successive bridges, tunnels and feeder journeys. Begin with rainfall, gradients and curves, then extend the analysis to station interchange and batch arrivals. Verify train running time separately from door-to-door journey time so that fast line-haul service is not mistaken for a complete passenger-experience result. The final submission should retain original inputs, measurement timestamps, uncertainty ranges and conclusions that the simplified expressions cannot establish.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b320-v16-s1","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度與沉陷差與軌道坡折","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity & Differential settlement and track kink","description":"本階段聚焦「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」與「沉陷差與軌道坡折」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" and \"Differential settlement and track kink\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b320-v16-01","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。 跨長四次方使幾何誤差特別重要，但只有在相同支承、均布荷載及截面條件下才可比較。將毫米轉成公尺後再核對剛度，可避免把量測位移誤差變成材料性能判斷。 在高架橋量測跨中及支點位移，區分彎曲與基礎移動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending. A railway bridge also requires dynamic and track-interaction checks; this static beam exercise only reveals parameter magnitudes. Fourth-power span dependence makes geometry important, but comparison requires the same support, uniform-load and section assumptions. Convert millimetres and metres consistently before checking stiffness, so a displacement-unit error does not become a false conclusion about material properties. Measure viaduct midspan and support displacement to distinguish bending from foundation movement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-01-k1","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity","text":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。","textEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" is correct?","options":["橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b320-v16-02","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：定量估算","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 28.875 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.616362 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 28.875 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.616362 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 28.875 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.616362 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 28.875 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.616362 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\", which statement holds?","options":["長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4。"],"optionsEn":["One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.25 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.103997 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b320-v16-03","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。","textEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\"?","options":["在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b320-v16-04","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在高架橋量測跨中及支點位移，區分彎曲與基礎移動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measure viaduct midspan and support displacement to distinguish bending from foundation movement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。","textEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b320-v16-05","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement and track kink” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。 相同端點坡度可以對應完全不同的中間形狀，因此坡度不能單獨表示軌道曲率。測點間距必須小於欲辨認的變形尺度，並將高程誤差相對於基長傳遞到坡度結果。 追蹤橋台與填土路基之間的差異沉陷長度尺度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉陷差與軌道坡折」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak. A spatial profile is needed to identify curvature and deformation length. Identical endpoint gradient can hide very different intermediate shapes, so gradient alone cannot describe track curvature. Survey spacing must resolve the deformation length scale, and elevation uncertainty must be propagated relative to the baseline into the reported gradient. Track the length scale of differential settlement between an abutment and filled earthworks. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement and track kink” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement and track kink”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-05-k1","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink","text":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。","textEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Differential settlement and track kink\" is correct?","options":["兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b320-v16-06","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：定量估算","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement and track kink” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.01386 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.693 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.01386 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.693 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.01386 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.693 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.01386 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.693 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Differential settlement and track kink\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.0126 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.63 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b320-v16-07","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement and track kink” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。","textEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Differential settlement and track kink\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b320-v16-08","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：失效診斷","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement and track kink” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：追蹤橋台與填土路基之間的差異沉陷長度尺度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Track the length scale of differential settlement between an abutment and filled earthworks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。","textEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉陷差與軌道坡折」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Differential settlement and track kink\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b320-v16-s2","title":"集水與排水容量與坡度阻力與爬坡功率","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity & Gradient resistance and climbing power","description":"本階段聚焦「集水與排水容量」與「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" and \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b320-v16-09","title":"集水與排水容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「集水與排水容量」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。 合理化流量法假定雨強與集流條件相符，面積及逕流係數也須明確。它估算峰值流率而非完整洪水歷線；抽水或蓄水設計還需對時間積分和出口條件。 比較短時強降雨與長時降雨對集水估算的不同假設。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水與排水容量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level. Counting only track surface can omit inflow from adjacent slopes and station areas. The rational estimate assumes rainfall intensity compatible with catchment response and explicit area and runoff coefficient. It gives a peak rate, not a complete hydrograph. Pumping or storage design additionally requires time integration and outlet conditions. Compare assumptions for short intense rainfall and longer rainfall in catchment estimates. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集水與排水容量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-09-k1","title":"集水與排水容量","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity","text":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。","textEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" is correct?","options":["短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b320-v16-10","title":"集水與排水容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集水與排水容量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.31e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.35343 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.31e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.35343 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.31e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.35343 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.31e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.35343 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集水與排水容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Original hypothetical exercise.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.1e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.3213 m^3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b320-v16-11","title":"集水與排水容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水與排水容量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。","textEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定","現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone.","Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater."],"answer":2,"explanation":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b320-v16-12","title":"集水與排水容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集水與排水容量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較短時強降雨與長時降雨對集水估算的不同假設。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare assumptions for short intense rainfall and longer rainfall in catchment estimates.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。","textEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集水與排水容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b320-v16-13","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gradient resistance and climbing power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。功率還與速度相乘，因此相同牽引力下高速爬坡更耗功率；下坡則需處理持續制動能量而非僅一次停車。 坡度以升高量除以水平距離表示，百分比與小數不可混用。此項只表示重力位能增加的速率，總牽引功率還要加上加速、滾動、氣動及轉換損失。 把山區坡度帶來的持續功率與加速功率分別列出。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. For small gradients, the along-track gravity force is approximately weight times gradient. Multiplication by speed gives power, making faster climbing more demanding at equal force; descending requires continuous energy management rather than merely one stopping event. Gradient is rise divided by horizontal distance, so percentage and decimal representations must not be mixed. This term only gives the rate of gravitational potential-energy increase. Total traction demand also includes acceleration, rolling resistance, aerodynamics and conversion losses. List sustained gradient power separately from acceleration power on a hillside section. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gradient resistance and climbing power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW.","failure":"常見誤解：「長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gradient resistance and climbing power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-13-k1","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power","text":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。功率還與速度相乘，因此相同牽引力下高速爬坡更耗功率；下坡則需處理持續制動能量而非僅一次停車。","textEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. For small gradients, the along-track gravity force is approximately weight times gradient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" is correct?","options":["長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動","列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.","Climbing raises gravitational potential energy.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車爬坡需提高重力位能，坡度小時沿線重力分量約等於重量乘坡度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Climbing raises gravitational potential energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b320-v16-14","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：定量估算","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gradient resistance and climbing power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 346500 kg，其餘固定，結果為 2719.332 kW。模型邊界：小坡度且定速；不含空阻、輪阻、加速與傳動損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 346500 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2719.332 kW. Model boundary: Small gradient and constant speed; aerodynamic drag, rolling resistance, acceleration and drive losses are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW。敏感度：mass 單獨增加百分之十至 346500 kg，其餘固定，結果為 2719.332 kW。模型邊界：小坡度且定速；不含空阻、輪阻、加速與傳動損失。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW. Sensitivity: mass, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 346500 kg, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2719.332 kW. Model boundary: Small gradient and constant speed; aerodynamic drag, rolling resistance, acceleration and drive losses are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\", which statement holds?","options":["隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s；計算：climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mass=315000 kg; gradient=0.02 1; v=40 m/s; calculation: climbing=mass*9.81*gradient*v/1000=2472.12 kW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b320-v16-15","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gradient resistance and climbing power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 由高程剖面核對坡度，使用同一時間窗比對速度與牽引功率，另列非重力負載。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Check gradient from the elevation profile, compare speed and traction power over one time window, and list non-gravitational loads separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用相同高差設計長緩坡與短陡坡，對比理想位能和峰值功率，指出兩者為何不能用同一項設備額定值評估。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 climbing，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design a long gentle and short steep climb with equal height gain, compare ideal energy and peak power, and explain why one equipment rating cannot evaluate both. Also recalculate climbing for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 由高程剖面核對坡度，使用同一時間窗比對速度與牽引功率，另列非重力負載。","textEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Check gradient from the elevation profile, compare speed and traction power over one time window, and list non-gravitational loads separately.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用相同高差設計長緩坡與短陡坡，對比理想位能和峰值功率，指出兩者為何不能用同一項設備額定值評估。 再以本單元 mass 的對照值重算 climbing，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Design a long gentle and short steep climb with equal height gain, compare ideal energy and peak power, and explain why one equipment rating cannot evaluate both. Also recalculate climbing for the alternative mass value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\"?","options":["以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以路線縱斷面和列車速度重建位能變化，對照受電功率積分；坡度資料與里程基準必須一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconstruct potential-energy change from the vertical alignment and train speed, compare it with integrated line power, and keep gradient and distance datums consistent. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b320-v16-16","title":"坡度阻力與爬坡功率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gradient resistance and climbing power: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gradient resistance and climbing power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 功率不足時須分辨坡度阻力與黏著限制，不能只加大電流。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. When power is insufficient, distinguish gradient resistance from adhesion limits rather than only increasing current. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把山區坡度帶來的持續功率與加速功率分別列出。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: List sustained gradient power separately from acceleration power on a hillside section.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 功率不足時須分辨坡度阻力與黏著限制，不能只加大電流。","textEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. When power is insufficient, distinguish gradient resistance from adhesion limits rather than only increasing current.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「坡度阻力與爬坡功率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gradient resistance and climbing power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略長下坡持續熱負荷會把短時煞車能力誤當連續能力；坡度正負號錯誤則會把耗能段當成回收段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring sustained downhill heat confuses short-term braking capability with continuous rating; a gradient-sign error can mislabel an energy-consuming section as regenerative. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b320-v16-s3","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度與地震偵測提前量","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration & Seismic detection lead time","description":"本階段聚焦「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」與「地震偵測提前量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" and \"Seismic detection lead time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b320-v16-17","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。超高平衡速度只對特定半徑和速度成立，慢車可能出現超高過剩；不能把增加超高當成所有車種都受益的措施。 殘餘加速度的正負表示側向作用方向，而不是安全與危險的二元判斷。半徑、軌距與高差必須使用一致長度單位，車體感受還會受到懸吊轉角影響。 比較曲線設計速度與降速通過情境的未平衡加速度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. Equilibrium cant applies to one radius and speed. A slower service can experience cant excess, so increasing cant does not improve every train condition. The sign of residual acceleration identifies its lateral direction, not a binary safe-unsafe outcome. Radius, gauge and rail-level difference require consistent length units. Carbody response is additionally affected by suspension rotation, which this geometric estimate does not resolve. Compare unbalanced acceleration at design speed and during a restricted-speed passage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cant and unbalanced acceleration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-17-k1","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration","text":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。超高平衡速度只對特定半徑和速度成立，慢車可能出現超高過剩；不能把增加超高當成所有車種都受益的措施。","textEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. Equilibrium cant applies to one radius and speed.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" is correct?","options":["任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b320-v16-18","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 69.3 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.4158225 m/s^2。模型邊界：小角度近似與剛性車體；未計懸吊側滾、動態輪重減載和規範允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 69.3 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.4158225 m/s^2. Model boundary: Small-angle approximation and rigid body; suspension roll, dynamic wheel unloading and acceptance limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 69.3 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.4158225 m/s^2。模型邊界：小角度近似與剛性車體；未計懸吊側滾、動態輪重減載和規範允收值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 69.3 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.4158225 m/s^2. Model boundary: Small-angle approximation and rigid body; suspension roll, dynamic wheel unloading and acceptance limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接","車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.","Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.20745 m/s^2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b320-v16-19","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 用實測半徑和高差重算平衡速度，保留感測器安裝角的校正值及量測不確定度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Recalculate equilibrium speed from measured radius and cant, retaining mounting-angle corrections and uncertainty for the acceleration sensor. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：選兩種速度共同計算殘餘加速度，找出符號反轉位置，說明為何混合服務需要速度分布而非單一最高速度。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 residual，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate residual acceleration for two speeds, locate its sign reversal, and explain why mixed services require a speed distribution rather than one maximum speed. Also recalculate residual for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 用實測半徑和高差重算平衡速度，保留感測器安裝角的校正值及量測不確定度。","textEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Recalculate equilibrium speed from measured radius and cant, retaining mounting-angle corrections and uncertainty for the acceleration sensor.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"選兩種速度共同計算殘餘加速度，找出符號反轉位置，說明為何混合服務需要速度分布而非單一最高速度。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 residual，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Calculate residual acceleration for two speeds, locate its sign reversal, and explain why mixed services require a speed distribution rather than one maximum speed. Also recalculate residual for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b320-v16-20","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需核對高差符號與曲線方向，防止左右軌互換。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Check cant sign against curve direction to prevent swapping the inner and outer rails. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較曲線設計速度與降速通過情境的未平衡加速度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare unbalanced acceleration at design speed and during a restricted-speed passage.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需核對高差符號與曲線方向，防止左右軌互換。","textEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Check cant sign against curve direction to prevent swapping the inner and outer rails.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b320-v16-21","title":"地震偵測提前量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「地震偵測提前量」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seismic detection lead time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。距離太近時提前量可能為負，警報並不能讓列車瞬間停止。 此處以相同距離比較兩種波速，屬簡化幾何模型。實際感測站可能不在線路與震源之間；可用時間還包括資料品質檢查及保護命令發送，不能只比較波速。 用不同震源距離檢查預警可用提前量，不宣稱可預測地震。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地震偵測提前量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. A nearby source may leave negative lead time. An alarm therefore cannot make a moving train stop instantaneously, even when the detection itself works correctly. The exercise compares two wave speeds over the same distance and therefore uses simplified geometry. A real sensor may not lie between the source and railway. Available time also includes data-quality checks and protection-command delivery, not only wave propagation. Check available lead time at different source distances without claiming earthquake prediction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seismic detection lead time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地震偵測提前量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seismic detection lead time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-21-k1","title":"地震偵測提前量","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time","text":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。距離太近時提前量可能為負，警報並不能讓列車瞬間停止。","textEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. A nearby source may leave negative lead time.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地震偵測提前量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seismic detection lead time\" is correct?","options":["地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b320-v16-22","title":"地震偵測提前量：定量估算","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地震偵測提前量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seismic detection lead time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 115500 m，其餘固定，結果為 11.75 s。模型邊界：共線源站幾何與固定波速；不預測震度或實際地震動。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 115500 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 11.75 s. Model boundary: Collinear source-station geometry and constant wave speeds; neither intensity nor actual ground motion is predicted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 115500 m，其餘固定，結果為 11.75 s。模型邊界：共線源站幾何與固定波速；不預測震度或實際地震動。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 115500 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 11.75 s. Model boundary: Collinear source-station geometry and constant wave speeds; neither intensity nor actual ground motion is predicted.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地震偵測提前量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seismic detection lead time\", which statement holds?","options":["兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time.","Original hypothetical exercise.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=105000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=10.5 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b320-v16-23","title":"地震偵測提前量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地震偵測提前量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seismic detection lead time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 以完整訊號重播核對每個時間戳，將總延遲分解成判定、網路與列車端處理。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Use full-chain signal replay to verify every timestamp and separate total delay into decision, network and train-side processing components. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將震源距離縮短並把通訊延遲加倍，計算剩餘提前量；與制動時間比較，提出只在模型範圍內成立的結論。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 lead，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Shorten source distance and double communication delay, calculate remaining lead time, and compare it with braking time without extending the conclusion beyond the model. Also recalculate lead for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 以完整訊號重播核對每個時間戳，將總延遲分解成判定、網路與列車端處理。","textEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Use full-chain signal replay to verify every timestamp and separate total delay into decision, network and train-side processing components.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將震源距離縮短並把通訊延遲加倍，計算剩餘提前量；與制動時間比較，提出只在模型範圍內成立的結論。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 lead，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Shorten source distance and double communication delay, calculate remaining lead time, and compare it with braking time without extending the conclusion beyond the model. Also recalculate lead for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地震偵測提前量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seismic detection lead time\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b320-v16-24","title":"地震偵測提前量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地震偵測提前量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seismic detection lead time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 感測成功不等於制動成功，須查列車收到命令後的動作。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Successful detection is not successful braking; inspect the train response after command receipt. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：用不同震源距離檢查預警可用提前量，不宣稱可預測地震。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check available lead time at different source distances without claiming earthquake prediction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 感測成功不等於制動成功，須查列車收到命令後的動作。","textEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Successful detection is not successful braking; inspect the train response after command receipt.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地震偵測提前量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seismic detection lead time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b320-v16-s4","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞與轉乘步行與銜接餘裕","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel & Transfer walking and connection margin","description":"本階段聚焦「隧道壓力波傳遞」與「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" and \"Transfer walking and connection margin\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b320-v16-25","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「隧道壓力波傳遞」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。 波傳時間由傳播距離除以聲速決定，與列車走完整段的時間不同。此式只預測到達時序而不預測波幅；洞口形狀、列車頭型和反射決定的壓力變化須用其他流動模型。 在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隧道壓力波傳遞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform. Wave arrival and train arrival are different events and require separate measurement triggers. Wave travel time is propagation distance divided by sound speed, not the time for the train to traverse the section. This expression predicts arrival timing, not amplitude. Portal geometry, train-nose shape and reflections require additional flow models to predict pressure changes. Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.720588 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.720588 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隧道壓力波傳遞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tunnel pressure-wave travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-25-k1","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel","text":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。","textEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" is correct?","options":["隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b320-v16-26","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：定量估算","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道壓力波傳遞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.720588 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2887.5 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.492647 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.720588 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2887.5 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.492647 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.720588 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2887.5 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.492647 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.720588 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2887.5 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.492647 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隧道壓力波傳遞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\", which statement holds?","options":["車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.720588 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2625 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.720588 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b320-v16-27","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。","textEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\"?","options":["在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b320-v16-28","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道壓力波傳遞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。","textEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隧道壓力波傳遞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。","轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak.","The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b320-v16-29","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transfer walking and connection margin” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。最短路徑不一定最快，因為樓梯、閘門與人流交會造成等待；無障礙路徑需要獨立列出而非套用同一速度。 距離除速度只表示行走或移動時間，等待列車、排隊和辨識路徑應另列。使用單一平均速度會掩蓋行李、行動能力和雙向干擾，應以分段分群資料檢查。 把接駁列車步行、等待和搭乘分成可核對的旅程段。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs. The shortest route is not always fastest because stairs, gates and crossing streams cause waiting. Accessible routes need their own timing rather than an assumed common walking speed. Distance divided by speed represents movement only; train waiting, queueing and wayfinding need separate terms. One mean speed hides baggage, mobility differences and opposing flow. Check the result with segmented measurements for relevant passenger groups. Split feeder walking, waiting and riding into independently verifiable journey stages. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transfer walking and connection margin” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transfer walking and connection margin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-29-k1","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin","text":"轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。最短路徑不一定最快，因為樓梯、閘門與人流交會造成等待；無障礙路徑需要獨立列出而非套用同一速度。","textEn":"A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs. The shortest route is not always fastest because stairs, gates and crossing streams cause waiting.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transfer walking and connection margin\" is correct?","options":["轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接","兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間","轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.","Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time.","A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"轉乘能否銜接取決於實際可用時間扣除下車、步行、垂直動線與候車需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A connection depends on available time after alighting, walking, vertical circulation and boarding needs. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b320-v16-30","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：定量估算","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transfer walking and connection margin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 m，其餘固定，結果為 47.1 s。模型邊界：固定步速與額外時間；不包含動態排隊或旅客個別差異分布。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 47.1 s. Model boundary: Fixed walking speed and additional time; dynamic queues and individual variability distributions are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 m，其餘固定，結果為 47.1 s。模型邊界：固定步速與額外時間；不包含動態排隊或旅客個別差異分布。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 47.1 s. Model boundary: Fixed walking speed and additional time; dynamic queues and individual variability distributions are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transfer walking and connection margin\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s；計算：margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: available=300 s; distance=189 m; speed=1 m/s; vertical=45 s; calculation: margin=available-distance/speed-vertical=66 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b320-v16-31","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transfer walking and connection margin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。 在路徑起終點對時，逐段記錄水平、垂直與等待時間，核對是否漏計驗票或排隊。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment. Synchronise route endpoints, record horizontal movement, vertical movement and waiting separately, and check for omitted gate processing or queues. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較一般與無障礙兩條路徑的餘裕，加入一台電梯停機情境，說明時刻表調整與空間導引分別能改善哪一段。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 margin，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare connection margins for ordinary and accessible routes, add one unavailable lift, and distinguish improvements from timetable changes versus spatial guidance. Also recalculate margin for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。 在路徑起終點對時，逐段記錄水平、垂直與等待時間，核對是否漏計驗票或排隊。","textEn":"Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment. Synchronise route endpoints, record horizontal movement, vertical movement and waiting separately, and check for omitted gate processing or queues.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較一般與無障礙兩條路徑的餘裕，加入一台電梯停機情境，說明時刻表調整與空間導引分別能改善哪一段。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 margin，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare connection margins for ordinary and accessible routes, add one unavailable lift, and distinguish improvements from timetable changes versus spatial guidance. Also recalculate margin for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transfer walking and connection margin\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以匿名實測旅程時間分位數比較路徑，記錄電梯等待及閘門排隊，檢查轉乘圖的距離是否包含所有垂直動線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare route-time quantiles from anonymous observations, record lift and gate waits, and check that route distances include every vertical circulation segment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b320-v16-32","title":"轉乘步行與銜接餘裕：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transfer walking and connection margin: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transfer walking and connection margin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 旅客走錯路會改變實際距離，需比較引導前後的路徑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. Wrong turns change actual distance; compare observed routes before and after guidance changes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把接駁列車步行、等待和搭乘分成可核對的旅程段。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Split feeder walking, waiting and riding into independently verifiable journey stages.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「轉乘路線距離最短就一定適合所有旅客最快銜接」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest transfer route necessarily gives every passenger the fastest connection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 旅客走錯路會改變實際距離，需比較引導前後的路徑。","textEn":"Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. Wrong turns change actual distance; compare observed routes before and after guidance changes.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「轉乘步行與銜接餘裕」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transfer walking and connection margin\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間","只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time.","Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只用最快步行者校準會低估多數人的轉乘時間；電梯停機又可能使唯一無障礙路徑失去連續性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calibrating to the fastest walkers understates many passengers’ transfer time; a failed lift can also break the only continuous accessible route. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b320-v16-s5","title":"到站變異與平均等候與周轉時間與車隊需求","titleEn":"Arrival variability and mean waiting & Round-trip time and fleet size","description":"本階段聚焦「到站變異與平均等候」與「周轉時間與車隊需求」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Arrival variability and mean waiting\" and \"Round-trip time and fleet size\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b320-v16-33","title":"到站變異與平均等候：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Arrival variability and mean waiting: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「到站變異與平均等候」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Arrival variability and mean waiting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"當旅客隨機到站且不受容量限制時，平均等待與班距平方的期望值有關，長班距被更多旅客遇到。兩組平均班距相同的服務仍可能有不同等待時間，因此準點與均勻性具有獨立價值。 隨機到站旅客更容易遇到較長班距，因為長區間占較多時間，因此平均等候與班距變異數有關。公式假定旅客到達獨立於班表且每班可上車，不能表示服務櫃台或容量不足的隊列。 比較接駁班距波動造成的隨機等候，批次到達另做事件模擬。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「到站變異與平均等候」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"With random passenger arrivals and no capacity constraint, mean waiting depends on the expected squared headway. More passengers encounter longer gaps. Services with identical mean headway can therefore have different waiting times, giving regularity a value separate from the average frequency. Random arrivals encounter longer headways more often because those intervals occupy more time. Mean waiting therefore depends on headway variance. The formula assumes arrivals independent of the timetable and successful boarding on every train; it does not model counters or capacity-constrained queues. Compare random waiting from feeder-headway variability and separately simulate batch arrivals. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Arrival variability and mean waiting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mean=189 s; sd=60 s；計算：wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mean=189 s; sd=60 s; calculation: wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「到站變異與平均等候」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Arrival variability and mean waiting”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-33-k1","title":"到站變異與平均等候","titleEn":"Arrival variability and mean waiting","text":"當旅客隨機到站且不受容量限制時，平均等待與班距平方的期望值有關，長班距被更多旅客遇到。兩組平均班距相同的服務仍可能有不同等待時間，因此準點與均勻性具有獨立價值。","textEn":"With random passenger arrivals and no capacity constraint, mean waiting depends on the expected squared headway. More passengers encounter longer gaps.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「到站變異與平均等候」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Arrival variability and mean waiting\" is correct?","options":["當旅客隨機到站且不受容量限制時，平均等待與班距平方的期望值有關，長班距被更多旅客遇到。","兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間","車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定"],"optionsEn":["With random passenger arrivals and no capacity constraint, mean waiting depends on the expected squared headway.","Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time.","Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"當旅客隨機到站且不受容量限制時，平均等待與班距平方的期望值有關，長班距被更多旅客遇到。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"With random passenger arrivals and no capacity constraint, mean waiting depends on the expected squared headway. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b320-v16-34","title":"到站變異與平均等候：定量估算","titleEn":"Arrival variability and mean waiting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「到站變異與平均等候」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Arrival variability and mean waiting” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mean=189 s; sd=60 s；計算：wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s。敏感度：mean 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 s，其餘固定，結果為 112.608 s。模型邊界：獨立隨機旅客到達、穩態班距且皆可登車；不含時刻表配合到站。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mean=189 s; sd=60 s; calculation: wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s. Sensitivity: mean, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 112.608 s. Model boundary: Random independent passenger arrivals, stationary headways and no denied boarding; timetable-aware arrivals are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從連續到站紀錄計算班距平均與變異數，再用匿名旅客到站時刻重播等待，檢查是否存在容量不足或非隨機到站。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calculate headway mean and variance from consecutive arrivals, replay waiting with anonymous passenger arrival times, and check for capacity limits or nonrandom arrivals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mean=189 s; sd=60 s；計算：wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s。敏感度：mean 單獨增加百分之十至 207.9 s，其餘固定，結果為 112.608 s。模型邊界：獨立隨機旅客到達、穩態班距且皆可登車；不含時刻表配合到站。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mean=189 s; sd=60 s; calculation: wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s. Sensitivity: mean, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 207.9 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 112.608 s. Model boundary: Random independent passenger arrivals, stationary headways and no denied boarding; timetable-aware arrivals are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「到站變異與平均等候」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Arrival variability and mean waiting\", which statement holds?","options":["兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mean=189 s; sd=60 s。","長下坡只需通過一次緊急停車試驗就能驗證持續制動"],"optionsEn":["Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Original hypothetical exercise.","One emergency stop test verifies continuous braking capability on a long descent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mean=189 s; sd=60 s；計算：wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mean=189 s; sd=60 s; calculation: wait=(mean**2+sd**2)/(2*mean)=104.0238 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b320-v16-35","title":"到站變異與平均等候：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Arrival variability and mean waiting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「到站變異與平均等候」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Arrival variability and mean waiting” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從連續到站紀錄計算班距平均與變異數，再用匿名旅客到站時刻重播等待，檢查是否存在容量不足或非隨機到站。 從逐列到站時間重建班距平均與標準差，將旅客隨機到達事件重播，核對等候樣本平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calculate headway mean and variance from consecutive arrivals, replay waiting with anonymous passenger arrival times, and check for capacity limits or nonrandom arrivals. Reconstruct mean and standard deviation from successive train arrivals, replay random passenger arrivals, and compare the sampled mean waiting time. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持平均班距不變，把標準差減半後重算等待，並用一組確定性到站時間說明公式假設何時失效。 再以本單元 mean 的對照值重算 wait，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hold mean headway fixed and halve its standard deviation, recalculate waiting, then use deterministic arrivals to show when the formula assumptions fail. Also recalculate wait for the alternative mean value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只報平均班距會低估不規則服務的等待；旅客配合時刻表到站時又不能直接套用隨機到站公式。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reporting only mean headway understates waiting under irregular service, while timetable-aware arrivals invalidate the random-arrival formula. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從連續到站紀錄計算班距平均與變異數，再用匿名旅客到站時刻重播等待，檢查是否存在容量不足或非隨機到站。 從逐列到站時間重建班距平均與標準差，將旅客隨機到達事件重播，核對等候樣本平均。","textEn":"Calculate headway mean and variance from consecutive arrivals, replay waiting with anonymous passenger arrival times, and check for capacity limits or nonrandom arrivals. Reconstruct mean and standard deviation from successive train arrivals, replay random passenger arrivals, and compare the sampled mean waiting time.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持平均班距不變，把標準差減半後重算等待，並用一組確定性到站時間說明公式假設何時失效。 再以本單元 mean 的對照值重算 wait，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Hold mean headway fixed and halve its standard deviation, recalculate waiting, then use deterministic arrivals to show when the formula assumptions fail. Also recalculate wait for the alternative mean value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「到站變異與平均等候」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Arrival variability and mean waiting\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","從連續到站紀錄計算班距平均與變異數，再用匿名旅客到站時刻重播等待，檢查是否存在容量不足或非隨機到站。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Calculate headway mean and variance from consecutive arrivals, replay waiting with anonymous passenger arrival times, and check for capacity limits or nonrandom arrivals."],"answer":2,"explanation":"從連續到站紀錄計算班距平均與變異數，再用匿名旅客到站時刻重播等待，檢查是否存在容量不足或非隨機到站。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calculate headway mean and variance from consecutive arrivals, replay waiting with anonymous passenger arrival times, and check for capacity limits or nonrandom arrivals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b320-v16-36","title":"到站變異與平均等候：失效診斷","titleEn":"Arrival variability and mean waiting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「到站變異與平均等候」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Arrival variability and mean waiting” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只報平均班距會低估不規則服務的等待；旅客配合時刻表到站時又不能直接套用隨機到站公式。 若滿載造成無法上車，需額外追蹤留下隊列而不能沿用公式。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reporting only mean headway understates waiting under irregular service, while timetable-aware arrivals invalidate the random-arrival formula. When full trains prevent boarding, track the remaining queue separately instead of reusing this formula. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較接駁班距波動造成的隨機等候，批次到達另做事件模擬。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare random waiting from feeder-headway variability and separately simulate batch arrivals.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩組平均班距相同就一定有相同平均等候時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two services with equal mean headway necessarily have equal mean passenger waiting time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只報平均班距會低估不規則服務的等待；旅客配合時刻表到站時又不能直接套用隨機到站公式。 若滿載造成無法上車，需額外追蹤留下隊列而不能沿用公式。","textEn":"Reporting only mean headway understates waiting under irregular service, while timetable-aware arrivals invalidate the random-arrival formula. When full trains prevent boarding, track the remaining queue separately instead of reusing this formula.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「到站變異與平均等候」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Arrival variability and mean waiting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只報平均班距會低估不規則服務的等待；旅客配合時刻表到站時又不能直接套用隨機到站公式。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定"],"optionsEn":["Reporting only mean headway understates waiting under irregular service, while timetable-aware arrivals invalidate the random-arrival formula.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只報平均班距會低估不規則服務的等待；旅客配合時刻表到站時又不能直接套用隨機到站公式。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reporting only mean headway understates waiting under irregular service, while timetable-aware arrivals invalidate the random-arrival formula. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b320-v16-37","title":"周轉時間與車隊需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Round-trip time and fleet size: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「周轉時間與車隊需求」如何影響雅萬高速鐵路的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Round-trip time and fleet size” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jakarta–Bandung high-speed railway”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"維持固定班距所需列車數取決於完整周轉時間除班距並向上取整，周轉包含兩端折返與停站。備用車和維修車需另列；只用單程行車時間會把車隊需求低估接近一半。 循環時間除以班距後必須向上取整，半列車不能提供完整班次。此數量是投入循環的最低值，維修備用、延誤緩衝與不同分支運轉仍需額外配置。 把接駁與高速列車班距分開排程，檢查整體銜接需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「周轉時間與車隊需求」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fleet requirement for fixed headway is round-trip cycle time divided by headway, rounded upward. The cycle includes terminal turnbacks and stops. Spares and maintenance vehicles are additional; using only one-way running time can underestimate the requirement by nearly half. Divide cycle time by headway and round upward because a fraction of a train cannot provide a full departure. This is the minimum circulating requirement; maintenance spares, delay buffers and branch-specific operation need additional allocation. Schedule feeder and high-speed headways separately and inspect connection requirements. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Round-trip time and fleet size” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains.","failure":"常見誤解：「車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「周轉時間與車隊需求」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Round-trip time and fleet size”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-37-k1","title":"周轉時間與車隊需求","titleEn":"Round-trip time and fleet size","text":"維持固定班距所需列車數取決於完整周轉時間除班距並向上取整，周轉包含兩端折返與停站。備用車和維修車需另列；只用單程行車時間會把車隊需求低估接近一半。","textEn":"Fleet requirement for fixed headway is round-trip cycle time divided by headway, rounded upward. The cycle includes terminal turnbacks and stops.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「周轉時間與車隊需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Round-trip time and fleet size\" is correct?","options":["車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定","維持固定班距所需列車數取決於完整周轉時間除班距並向上取整，周轉包含兩端折返與停站。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone.","Fleet requirement for fixed headway is round-trip cycle time divided by headway, rounded upward.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"維持固定班距所需列車數取決於完整周轉時間除班距並向上取整，周轉包含兩端折返與停站。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fleet requirement for fixed headway is round-trip cycle time divided by headway, rounded upward. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b320-v16-38","title":"周轉時間與車隊需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Round-trip time and fleet size: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「周轉時間與車隊需求」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Round-trip time and fleet size” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。敏感度：cycle 單獨增加百分之十至 6237 s，其餘固定，結果為 35 trains。模型邊界：固定周轉與班距、無延誤；不含備用率和維修排程。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains. Sensitivity: cycle, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 6237 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 35 trains. Model boundary: Fixed cycle and headway without delays; reserve ratio and maintenance scheduling are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐列串接實際到發時間檢查周轉，將折返與等待分開，並對尖峰班距需求與可出車數建立同一時點的清單。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Join actual arrival and departure logs by train, separate turnback from waiting, and compare peak headway requirements with trains available at the same time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。敏感度：cycle 單獨增加百分之十至 6237 s，其餘固定，結果為 35 trains。模型邊界：固定周轉與班距、無延誤；不含備用率和維修排程。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains. Sensitivity: cycle, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 6237 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 35 trains. Model boundary: Fixed cycle and headway without delays; reserve ratio and maintenance scheduling are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「周轉時間與車隊需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Round-trip time and fleet size\", which statement holds?","options":["排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5670 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b320-v16-39","title":"周轉時間與車隊需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Round-trip time and fleet size: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「周轉時間與車隊需求」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Round-trip time and fleet size” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐列串接實際到發時間檢查周轉，將折返與等待分開，並對尖峰班距需求與可出車數建立同一時點的清單。 核對往返與折返時間使用同一單位，以逐列時刻表重播，檢查每次發車是否有車可用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Join actual arrival and departure logs by train, separate turnback from waiting, and compare peak headway requirements with trains available at the same time. Verify consistent units for round-trip and turnaround times, replay a train-by-train timetable, and check vehicle availability at every departure. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：增加一端折返時間後重算車隊，檢查向上取整造成的跳變，再提出維修備用與臨時故障應如何另列。 再以本單元 cycle 的對照值重算 fleet，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase one terminal turnback time, recalculate fleet and examine rounding jumps, then explain separate allowances for maintenance reserve and unexpected failures. Also recalculate fleet for the alternative cycle value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐列串接實際到發時間檢查周轉，將折返與等待分開，並對尖峰班距需求與可出車數建立同一時點的清單。 核對往返與折返時間使用同一單位，以逐列時刻表重播，檢查每次發車是否有車可用。","textEn":"Join actual arrival and departure logs by train, separate turnback from waiting, and compare peak headway requirements with trains available at the same time. Verify consistent units for round-trip and turnaround times, replay a train-by-train timetable, and check vehicle availability at every departure.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"增加一端折返時間後重算車隊，檢查向上取整造成的跳變，再提出維修備用與臨時故障應如何另列。 再以本單元 cycle 的對照值重算 fleet，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase one terminal turnback time, recalculate fleet and examine rounding jumps, then explain separate allowances for maintenance reserve and unexpected failures. Also recalculate fleet for the alternative cycle value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「周轉時間與車隊需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Round-trip time and fleet size\"?","options":["逐列串接實際到發時間檢查周轉，將折返與等待分開，並對尖峰班距需求與可出車數建立同一時點的清單。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Join actual arrival and departure logs by train, separate turnback from waiting, and compare peak headway requirements with trains available at the same time.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐列串接實際到發時間檢查周轉，將折返與等待分開，並對尖峰班距需求與可出車數建立同一時點的清單。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Join actual arrival and departure logs by train, separate turnback from waiting, and compare peak headway requirements with trains available at the same time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b320-v16-40","title":"周轉時間與車隊需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Round-trip time and fleet size: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b320-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「周轉時間與車隊需求」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Round-trip time and fleet size” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 循環時間稍增可能跨過整數門檻，不能只比較百分比。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. A small cycle-time increase can cross an integer fleet threshold; percentages alone are insufficient. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把接駁與高速列車班距分開排程，檢查整體銜接需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Schedule feeder and high-speed headways separately and inspect connection requirements.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「車隊需求可以只用單程時間除以班距決定」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fleet requirement can be determined using one-way time divided by headway alone.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b320-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 循環時間稍增可能跨過整數門檻，不能只比較百分比。","textEn":"Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. A small cycle-time increase can cross an integer fleet threshold; percentages alone are insufficient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]},{"id":"b320-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「周轉時間與車隊需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Round-trip time and fleet size\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-b320-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b320-background"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b320-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b320-en.svg"}};
